 "method_limits": [
  "resolution is static: an import that resolves to a file does not prove the call returns an instance of the class, so H is an upper bound on readers of that class",
  "only a plain name or a module-qualified name is resolved; a call on an attribute of an imported object, on a subscript, or on a chained call is published as residue rather than guessed",
  "a receiver name assigned several calls module-wide is graded on the first call that resolves in-tree; control flow is not modelled, so the same limit E450 publishes applies here",
  "sibling imports (`import e437_name_recall` from a script beside it) and dotted imports are both tried; a module string that matches more than one corpus file is published as ambiguous instead of resolved by preference",
  "the module universe is this study's corpus, so an import of a file outside it reads as not in tree -- that is a statement about the scan, not about the repository",
  "the headline is a zero, so the face publishes a resolver control over the whole corpus (every assignment whose value is a call to a plain or qualified name): if that control ever reads zero, the zero in the headline is an instrument failure, not a reading",
  "the study's own smoke leg lives in smoke_test.py, a shared file the population already includes; the handful of call rows the leg adds are counted as growth rather than excluded, because carving one study's lines out of a shared file would make the population depend on who is reading it"
 ],
